<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61980" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάρος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], ὁ</span>, a ravenous sea-bird, perh.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sea-mew, gull</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				542b17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				593b3
			</span></i>: hence, metaph., of greedy demagogues, as Cleon, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. κεχηνὼς ἐπὶ πέτρας δημηγορῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					956
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κλέωνα τὸν λ. δώρων ἑλόντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					591
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				567
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Matro
				<u>Conv.</u>
				9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Timocl.
				4.9
			</span></i>; also of fools, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				12
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				913
			</span></i>.</div>
